  <div class="container">
    <h1>The Writing Hall</h1>

    <div class="intro">
      <p>
        Over the years I’ve written short stories, essays, opinions, and ideas across many different themes —
        sports (I was once published on the BBC), science, sociology, religion, politics, and geopolitics.
      </p>

      <p>
        My short stories have appeared at <em>The Junction</em>. I’ve self‑published children’s stories, two short stories,
        and a collection of poems around a decade ago. These can be found at:
        <br>
        <a href="https://www.lulu.com/search?contributor=Richard+Jenkins&page=1&pageSize=10&adult_audience_rating=00&sortBy=PRODUCT_SALES_90_DAYS" target="_blank">
          My Lulu Publications
        </a>
      </p>

      <p>
        I was a fringe member of the Medway Poets — although I didn’t know it at the time — and read my poems at the
        Medway Arts Centre in Chatham from around 1984 to 1989.
      </p>

      <p>
        This hall gathers those threads. Three rooms lie ahead, each holding a different kind of silence.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="sections">
      <a class="section" href="/writing/prose/index.html">
        <h2>Prose Chamber</h2>
        <p>Stories, fragments, dream‑paths, and quiet narratives.</p>
      </a>

      <a class="section" href="/writing/poems/index.html">
        <h2>Poetry Alcove</h2>
        <p>Verses, atmospheres, and the soft dust of memory.</p>
      </a>

      <a class="section" href="/writing/opinions/index.html">
        <h2>Opinions Gallery</h2>
        <p>Reflections, commentary, and thoughts that echo against stone.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
